{
	"$comment": "Ticket 16: the identity registries, read whole. A single response is capped at 5000 rows (measured: a limit of 20000 returned exactly 5000), and offset paging over a non-unique order loses rows at page boundaries (measured: it dropped the Teams page GIGABYTE Marines, which the rename chain needs), so the tables are partitioned by AllName ranges instead: a range partition cannot skip a row. `limit` stays at the server's cap; a bucket that comes back at 5000 is split further.",
